<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of Montefeltro</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The House of Montefeltro was an Italian noble family that ruled Urbino and the mountainous Montefeltro district on the borders of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romagna">Romagna</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marche">Marche</a> from the 13th century until 1508. Its members were Ghibelline captains and condottieri, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/federico-da-montefeltro">Federico da Montefeltro</a> became the first Duke of Urbino in 1474. When the line died out with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guidobaldo-da-montefeltro">Guidobaldo da Montefeltro</a> in 1508, Urbino passed to the della Rovere.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/house-of-montefeltro.jpg" alt="House of Montefeltro" width="320" height="363" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Facquis · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_arms_of_da_Montefeltro.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
